# Rust / Cargo build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
fuzz/target/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/artifacts/
# `mise run mutants` writes under out/, but a bare `cargo mutants` with no
# --output drops its copied trees and logs into a mutants.out/ beside whatever
# it was run from. No leading slash, so these match at any depth rather than
# only at the repo root — a run started from inside crates/<name>/ leaves one
# there instead.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# proptest counterexamples are **tracked**, not ignored, and there is no rule
# for them here on purpose. A `proptest-regressions/` file is a failing case the
# suite found by itself and then shrank -- the one test input that cannot be
# regenerated on demand -- so it is committed and replayed on every later run.
# Every proptest in the workspace is configured to write there
# (docs/10-cross-cutting/testing.md section 2).
#
# A flat `<name>.proptest-regressions` beside a test file is therefore not
# ignored either: it means that proptest is missing its `failure_persistence`
# setting and fell back to proptest's `WithSource` shape. It should show up in
# `git status` so the config gets fixed, rather than being hidden.

# Byte-compiled output from the CI gates in .github/scripts/, which are Python.
# Written whenever one is imported or executed, and they are run by hand as
# often as by CI. Same reasoning as above for the missing leading slash.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local vault data (dev/test)
.sunrise-vault/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Apple client build outputs (`mise run apple-xcframework`). Generated from the
# Rust source on every build; committing them would let the Swift bindings
# drift from the crate that defines them.
/build/
/out/

# Generated by `mise run macos-app` from apps/apple/project.yml, which is the
# committed source of truth for the Xcode project.
apps/apple/*.xcodeproj

# Generated by `mise run macos-app` from apps/apple/project.yml, alongside the
# .xcodeproj. Holds the `sunrise://` URL-scheme registration.
apps/apple/Generated/

# LLVM raw coverage profiles. `gatherCoverageData` is on in the UI-test
# schemes, and an instrumented process writes its profile to the working
# directory on exit — so every `mise run macos-uitest` used to dirty the tree.
*.profraw
*.profdata
